invariant: INV-26
file: quic_packet.c
catches: quic_suite_test_extern
reason: AES header protection keys its cipher at AES-128's 16 bytes under
  every AES suite, so a TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 connection masks its
  packet numbers with half its "quic hp" key. RFC 9001 section 5.4.3
  runs header protection with the AEAD's own AES, AES-256 there, so the
  peer computes another mask and every Handshake and 1-RTT packet fails
  to unprotect. This is the device path, which expands the key at each
  mask; inv26-quic-hp-stored-key-cut-to-aes128 is the host path.
  quic_suite_test_extern compares an AES-256 packet byte for byte
  with an independent computation; quic_packet_suite proves the length.

--- old
        aes_traffic_key_of(&k, 0, h->stored, h->schedule, h->key, suite_key_len(h->suite));
--- new
        aes_traffic_key_of(&k, 0, h->stored, h->schedule, h->key, AES_128_KEY);
